email.task:
You are an IT assistant. Tom, a new office assistant, needs to order toner cartridges for the office printers from the OfficeSupply website. Write an email to Tom explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- at least one comparative or superlative (more pages than, cheaper than, the cheapest);
- the verbs cost or come to to talk about the price;
- at least one recommendation (I recommend…, I think it's best to…);
- at least one indirect question (Could you ask … whether…?, Do you know if…?).
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
